hexagon: retry a dspqueue read or write that a signal interrupts
Fold-into: upstream/hexagon-host

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus every patch of the series before this one.

A signal to the thread of the host can stop a dspqueue_read or a
dspqueue_write while it waits. The call then gives AEE_EINTERRUPTED (46,
0x2e) and moves no packet. The Hexagon SDK tells the host to do such a
call again (stddef/AEEStdErr.h: "the user should return to the HLOS and
retry the call"). flush_pending did the read again only for AEE_EEXPIRED
and AEE_EWOULDBLOCK, and flush_batch did no write again. Thus the host
stopped with "dspqueue_read failed: 0x0000002e" or "dspqueue_write failed".

On the phone, fuzz_npu_decode with SIGURG (a no-op handler without
SA_RESTART) to the thread of the decodes every 2 ms stopped at the first
decode with this abort. The same replay with no signal passed 319 runs.
The SIGALRM timer of libFuzzer (-timeout=30) gave the same abort. The app
has the same host code, thus a signal without SA_RESTART to its decode
thread can stop the app.

The dspqueue library also gives AEE_EINTERRUPTED after a permanent failure
of the queue, for example when the DSP process stops. The library cancels
each wait of the queue, and after that each call gives the code
immediately. Then it calls the error callback of the queue on a different
thread (error_callback() and wait_signal_locked() in
src/dspqueue/dspqueue_cpu.c of github.com/quic/fastrpc). Thus a host that
does each interrupted call again with no limit does not stop, and its
thread uses a full CPU core.

This patch sets an error callback on the queue of each session. The
library calls it on a different thread. Thus the callback keeps the code
in queue_error, a std::atomic<int32_t>, with a release store. The read
loop and the two writes read queue_error with an acquire load, and they do
the call again for AEE_EINTERRUPTED only while it is 0. After the error
callback, they stop the process as before, and the abort message also
gives the code of the callback.

An interrupted write moves no packet, because the library copies the packet
only after it gets space in the queue. Thus a write that the host does
again sends the batch one time.

The callback writes no log line, because the library also calls it at a
regular exit of the process. The destructor of the FastRPC library stops
the DSP process, and the dspqueue library then calls the error callback of
each open queue with AEE_ENOSUCH (0x27). The app and fuzz_npu_decode do not
call dspqueue_close: the session stays until the process exits. A callback
that writes the code to the log gives a line at each exit. On the phone,
each log of such a build ended with "ggml-hex: HTP0 dspqueue error:
0x00000027" after the summary of the run.

A regular dspqueue_close gives no error callback. It sets the queue to
INVALID_QUEUE before it cancels the waits, and error_callback() skips such
a queue.

On the phone, with this patch, the replays of the failed corpus with SIGURG
every 2 ms and every 1 ms passed 319 runs each (2999 logit checks, no
abort). The seed run with -timeout=30 for 80 s passed 1119 runs (11029
logit checks, no abort). No log has a "dspqueue" line, and each log ends
with the summary of the run.

On the success path, each write compares one more value, thus the speed of
the decode does not change. The test mode of the hexhost harness gives
AEE_EINTERRUPTED to each third dspqueue_read and dspqueue_write
(HEXHOST_EINTR=3 of the fake DSP). Without this patch, 11 of the 14 graph
inputs and 9 of the 12 model graph paths stop with 0x2e, in the release
none and the debug ubsan builds. With this patch, all of them pass.

The check queue-cancel of the harness (HEXHOST_EINTR=cancel:2) stops the
queue of the fake DSP, and the fake DSP calls the error callback 2 ms
later. With this patch, the host stops with "dspqueue_read failed:
0x0000002e (queue error 0x00000027)". A host that does the call again with
no error callback does not stop before the timeout of libFuzzer. At the
exit of the process, the fake DSP calls the error callback of each open
queue, as the FastRPC library does. hexhost_graphs then gives no
"dspqueue" line with this patch, and it gives the line of the exit with a
callback that writes to the log.

